IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr5-sch6`

-- TESTS for Schedule 6 (Meaning of "relevant requirement"), lines 3256-3348.  Every expected value is
-- decided from the lists in the text before the run: an Article or regulation is in a list or it is not;
-- the chapeau's "means" makes a requirement in no list the text's no; the 14th and 15th printed paragraphs
-- (regulations 66 to 78 and 84(1)) lie after the last number the chapeau cites ("5 to 13") and answer
-- NOTHING under limb (b) (fork S6-F1).  The unwritten convention in the names below is the Article or the
-- regulation and then, after a comma, the paragraph ("" for none).

§ `Schedule 6 -- fixtures`

-- A requirement of these Regulations imposed on any other person (a relevant person, say).
GIVEN n IS A STRING
      p IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 requirement`
`sch 6 test: regulation` MEANS `sch 6 requirement` OF `sch 6 these Regulations`, n, p, `sch 6 any other person`

-- A requirement of these Regulations imposed on someone in particular.
GIVEN who IS A `sch 6 bearer`
      n IS A STRING
      p IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 requirement`
`sch 6 test: regulation on` MEANS `sch 6 requirement` OF `sch 6 these Regulations`, n, p, who

-- An Article of the funds transfer regulation imposed on someone in particular.
GIVEN who IS A `sch 6 bearer`
      n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 requirement`
`sch 6 test: Article on` MEANS `sch 6 requirement` OF `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation`, n, "", who

-- A regulation of the UK auctioning regulations imposed on someone in particular.
GIVEN who IS A `sch 6 bearer`
      n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 requirement`
`sch 6 test: UK auctioning regulation on` MEANS `sch 6 requirement` OF `sch 6 the UK auctioning regulations`, n, "", who


